  {"date": "2009-11-24", "venue": "Wachovia Center", "city": "Philadelphia", "state": "PA", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "prev": "Camel Walk", "next": "The Wedge", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2009-12-30", "venue": "American Airlines Arena", "city": "Miami", "state": "FL", "gap": 10, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "Sand", "next": "Lifeboy", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2010-10-16", "venue": "North Charleston Coliseum", "city": "North Charleston", "state": "SC", "gap": 35, "set": "1", "out": ">", "prev": "Guelah Papyrus", "next": "The Mango Song", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2010-10-26", "venue": "Verizon Wireless Arena", "city": "Manchester", "state": "NH", "gap": 5, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The Curtain bristles with crisp energy and is tightly rendered, with Mike and Fish seeming to propel the opening section. The animated jam in With also seems to bound along at a slighly quicker clip than the usual, more languid pace. Again, Fish and Mike drive the tempo, while Trey offers inspired and rapid-fire melodies. A high octane version.", "out": ">", "prev": "All of These Dreams", "next": "Scent of a Mule", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2011-06-10", "venue": "Susquehanna Bank Center", "city": "Camden", "state": "NJ", "gap": 18, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "There are a few spots here and there in The Curtain and the beginning of With that seem a bit off. Nonetheless, Trey soloing in With seems particularly inspired, and Mike is also noticeably strong. The jam reaches a fairly intense peak, before expectedly settling to conclude.", "prev": "The Sloth", "xnext": "Down with Disease", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2012-06-28", "venue": "Klipsch Music Center", "city": "Noblesville", "state": "IN", "gap": 38, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The Curtain section is well-executed, with notably strong Mike and Fish. The With jam features great Trey and Page interplay - not exactly call and response, but Trey plays a few licks, then Page responds with thoughts of his own. As the jam develops, they play simultaneously, each offering similar, yet distinct musical collages, while Fish and Mike adeptly keep the rhythm machine chugging along. A solid version start to finish.", "prev": "The Birdwatcher", "next": "Fuck Your Face", "nb": 1},
